WEBVTT

1
00:46:10.754 --> 00:46:17.534
Are there people on vacation who are guests in this church today?

2
00:46:17.534 --> 00:46:25.454
Are there vacationers here today? Let's give a round of applause for our brothers and sisters.

3
00:46:25.454 --> 00:46:34.874
Where do you come from? Purmerend. Yes, you can't help that.

4
00:46:34.874 --> 00:46:38.754
Real estate is cheaper here by the way. Hallelujah.

5
00:46:38.754 --> 00:46:45.234
Are there people here for the first time, just visiting? Yes, over there, let's give a round of applause.

6
00:46:45.234 --> 00:46:54.914
Thank you very much. Over there too. Where do you come from? From Peer, that's nearby.

7
00:46:54.914 --> 00:46:58.914
Good job. Welcome, welcome to Open Church. Hallelujah.

8
00:46:58.914 --> 00:47:06.954
Once again, the children are at camp and we set everything up yesterday.

9
00:47:06.954 --> 00:47:17.634
And I can truly say with gratitude that the team, set-up, pack-down, the children's team, the youth team,

10
00:47:17.634 --> 00:47:23.074
it has really become a well-oiled machine. And it is so nice to be able to work together.

11
00:47:23.074 --> 00:47:30.074
We started yesterday at 9 o'clock. There have been years when we started at 7 o'clock and only finished at 1 o'clock at night.

12
00:47:30.074 --> 00:47:37.754
Nowadays we start at 9 in the morning and it's relaxed, it goes quickly, it goes well, it's safe.

13
00:47:37.754 --> 00:47:43.194
And I am so happy with the team. Can we please give a round of applause for all the people?

14
00:47:43.194 --> 00:47:48.834
And it's all volunteer work. It's all volunteer work.

15
00:47:48.834 --> 00:47:54.914
And I was thinking about it this week and I thought to myself, for example, children's workers,

16
00:47:54.914 --> 00:48:00.994
and I mean seriously, we can find this funny, but I thought, why do people do this?

17
00:48:00.994 --> 00:48:11.594
Why would you go to children's camp? You know? And then take vacation days for it, so it's also costly.

18
00:48:11.594 --> 00:48:19.474
And it makes you tired and it gets you dirty. And it's not always safe, but it is safe.

19
00:48:19.514 --> 00:48:25.314
But why do people do this? Seriously, what drives us to do this?

20
00:48:25.314 --> 00:48:32.674
We do it for Jesus, but that intrinsic motivation really has to be there, driven by the Holy Spirit.

21
00:48:32.674 --> 00:48:37.514
And I can tell you, I can tell you, I have been to camp my whole life,

22
00:48:37.514 --> 00:48:41.394
but I have many memories of camp.

23
00:48:41.394 --> 00:48:53.714
But I think, and here it comes, it is much more complex and it goes much deeper, the effect, than just my memories.

24
00:48:53.714 --> 00:49:01.874
If it were only memories, then the effect might be good, but I believe, and that is what the arrow says,

25
00:49:01.874 --> 00:49:11.274
I believe that it goes much deeper, namely that the effect reaches much further than what I can imagine.

26
00:49:11.314 --> 00:49:22.434
Yes, I had great times. Put on your armor, and there were camps, and Chris here, there were youth leaders, children's leaders,

27
00:49:22.434 --> 00:49:31.474
and I literally looked up to him, because that guy was already two meters tall then, and I looked up to him, what a guy.

28
00:49:31.474 --> 00:49:38.674
There is really a guy here. That is really a dude, that is really an oak tree in God's kingdom.

29
00:49:38.674 --> 00:49:45.194
And you know, this morning I was driving with my children, with Joshua and Olivia, I was driving to the children's camp,

30
00:49:45.194 --> 00:49:51.954
and then Joshua said, oh, I hope, I hope that I am in Roy's group.

31
00:49:51.954 --> 00:49:56.474
I said, really? That's the drummer, you know.

32
00:49:56.474 --> 00:50:05.994
Oh yes, I hope, and I said, why do you want to be in Roy's group? He said, yes, I think Roy is just amazing.

33
00:50:05.994 --> 00:50:12.794
And then I think to myself, what makes Roy do that?

34
00:50:12.794 --> 00:50:24.514
But, just as he raised me in Christ, Roy is now raising my children in Christ.

35
00:50:24.514 --> 00:50:33.474
And I am raising my children, the first primary task of raising in Christ lies with the parents, but also the church.

36
00:50:33.474 --> 00:50:45.914
And that such a boy as Roy can be a role model for Joshua, God bless Joshua, that is worthy of eternity, that is worthy of eternity.

37
00:50:45.914 --> 00:50:54.474
And that Roy can then say about Joshua who he is, according to Scripture, not according to personal opinion, that is really nice, according to Scripture.

38
00:50:54.474 --> 00:51:00.634
That Roy can speak Scripture over my son. Go ahead, Roy, go for it.

39
00:51:00.634 --> 00:51:05.634
This is why we do children's camp. And this is why we have youth camp in a few days.

40
00:51:05.634 --> 00:51:18.234
And I think it's so cool that we have a whopping, what was it, how many? How many teenagers? 60 teenagers. I love it, I love it.

41
00:51:18.234 --> 00:51:23.834
And you know, we are a Holy Spirit filled church, amen.

42
00:51:23.834 --> 00:51:33.634
And what I actually want to say with that is this. Please people, I understand that people are working and we are busy with everything, but can I ask something of us?

43
00:51:33.634 --> 00:51:44.434
Please, whenever you think of it this week, just when the camp crosses your mind, pray for a moment. Shall we agree on that?

44
00:51:44.434 --> 00:51:50.234
Just pray. Just a minute here and before you go to bed and fall asleep, oh, how would it be this time?

45
00:51:50.234 --> 00:51:59.434
Pray. Pray in tongues. Just pray for the camp. Pray for the filling of the Holy Spirit. Pray for safety. Pray for the spiritual battle.

46
00:51:59.434 --> 00:52:08.434
You know, Debbie told me yesterday things about what she used to do as a children's worker and that she prayed over a camp.

47
00:52:08.434 --> 00:52:15.434
And she said, we are releasing in the spiritual world what had happened for this camp at this address.

48
00:52:15.434 --> 00:52:21.434
And she talked about certain, dirty, hostile, anti-Christian matters.

49
00:52:21.434 --> 00:52:25.434
She didn't know that, but she was just breaking it in Jesus' name.

50
00:52:25.434 --> 00:52:35.434
And later the camp location manager said to Debbie, thank you, you have been such a good camp.

51
00:52:35.434 --> 00:52:40.434
And the contrast was so great, because before you there was a certain group.

52
00:52:40.434 --> 00:52:49.434
And they named exactly the sinfulness and the anti-Christianity and the filth that Debbie had prayed about at the beginning of that camp.

53
00:52:49.434 --> 00:52:50.434
Do you understand what I mean?

54
00:52:50.434 --> 00:52:56.434
And therefore, we are spirit, soul, and body, but do not underestimate the spiritual world.

55
00:52:56.434 --> 00:52:58.434
And therefore we must pray. Amen?

56
00:52:58.434 --> 00:52:59.434
Amen.

57
00:52:59.434 --> 00:53:00.434
Thank you guys. Thank you.

58
00:53:00.434 --> 00:53:03.434
Bram, may I invite you to the stage for the offering?

59
00:53:06.434 --> 00:53:12.434
Good morning. I don't have much more to add. Let's read the text.

60
00:53:15.434 --> 00:53:21.434
As we have this week, this is being a congregation at its turbo.

61
00:53:23.434 --> 00:53:31.434
This is together as a congregation caring for the maturity of children and young people.

62
00:53:32.434 --> 00:53:33.434
Father.

63
00:53:36.434 --> 00:53:47.434
This is a text that Paul wrote, after he explained how through Jesus Christ everything, everything, everything changes.

64
00:53:48.434 --> 00:53:53.434
And how Jesus Christ has achieved a total victory.

65
00:53:53.434 --> 00:54:00.434
And as we realize this, Paul concludes, and he says this to us as well,

66
00:54:00.434 --> 00:54:04.434
be therefore always strong in the faith.

67
00:54:05.434 --> 00:54:11.434
Dear brothers and sisters, shall we always be strong in the faith?

68
00:54:12.434 --> 00:54:13.434
Persevere!

69
00:54:14.434 --> 00:54:17.434
There is a reason, sometimes it does not come naturally, it does not stand for nothing.

70
00:54:17.434 --> 00:54:18.434
Persevere!

71
00:54:19.434 --> 00:54:22.434
For we must keep our eyes on Jesus, on the eternal future.

72
00:54:22.434 --> 00:54:25.434
Persevere, always do your best for the Lord.

73
00:54:26.434 --> 00:54:32.434
There are many people this week who are working very hard for the Lord.

74
00:54:33.434 --> 00:54:40.434
You must know that everything you do for the Lord will be rewarded.

75
00:54:43.434 --> 00:54:45.434
I have nothing more to add to that.

76
00:54:45.434 --> 00:54:50.434
What we do for the Lord is of course the camps that we as a church have also financially,

77
00:54:51.434 --> 00:54:54.434
yes that was last week, financially supported.

78
00:54:56.434 --> 00:54:59.434
Shall we also contribute financially now?

79
00:54:59.434 --> 00:55:01.434
That is also what you do for the Lord.

80
00:55:01.434 --> 00:55:09.434
That can be done via the app, it can be done via QR codes, it can simply be done through a bank transfer,

81
00:55:09.434 --> 00:55:11.434
the data list is on the card.

82
00:55:11.434 --> 00:55:16.434
If someone is a guest, feel free, be a guest.

83
00:55:16.434 --> 00:55:18.434
If you want to contribute, welcome.

84
00:55:19.434 --> 00:55:23.434
Let it pass you by for a moment, just as welcome.

85
00:55:23.434 --> 00:55:28.434
As a congregation we say, we carry it together.

86
00:55:28.434 --> 00:55:30.434
In the name of Jesus, amen.

87
00:55:40.434 --> 00:55:42.434
Are we ready for God's Word?

88
00:55:43.434 --> 00:55:45.434
Hallelujah, grab your Bible.

89
00:55:47.434 --> 00:55:49.434
Then we will begin.

90
00:55:54.434 --> 00:56:02.434
Last week I preached, I would say, part 1 of 2.

91
00:56:05.434 --> 00:56:11.434
And last week the entire service actually lasted only the introduction.

92
00:56:13.434 --> 00:56:16.434
While I actually prefer to teach the Bible.

93
00:56:16.434 --> 00:56:19.434
So today we are going to do Bible study, if that’s alright with you.

94
00:56:20.434 --> 00:56:26.434
I spoke last week about sanctification, purification and consecration.

95
00:56:26.434 --> 00:56:27.434
Do you still remember those?

96
00:56:29.434 --> 00:56:33.434
Michels, can we take a look at those words again?

97
00:56:33.434 --> 00:56:38.434
So it's sanctification, purification and consecration.

98
00:56:38.434 --> 00:56:42.434
And then in Dutch we take the same words.

99
00:56:42.434 --> 00:56:44.434
I have set them down well this time.

100
00:56:44.434 --> 00:56:48.434
Sanctification, purification and consecration.

101
00:56:49.434 --> 00:57:02.434
What I started with last week is to tell you that we have been freed from the guilt that was upon us by the blood of Jesus.

102
00:57:02.434 --> 00:57:05.434
Jesus has freed us.

103
00:57:05.434 --> 00:57:09.434
And whoever is freed by Jesus is truly free. Amen?

104
00:57:10.434 --> 00:57:16.434
And what Jesus has done for us, we cannot add anything to it.

105
00:57:16.434 --> 00:57:20.434
We cannot save ourselves.

106
00:57:20.434 --> 00:57:21.434
That is not possible.

107
00:57:21.434 --> 00:57:24.434
That is 100% Jesus.

108
00:57:24.434 --> 00:57:30.434
Jesus did what was necessary, what no one could do.

109
00:57:30.434 --> 00:57:33.434
That is why we just sang, worthy is the lamb.

110
00:57:33.434 --> 00:57:39.434
Because no one, absolutely no one, could do what Jesus has done.

111
00:57:39.434 --> 00:57:44.434
To remain perfect, to remain obedient to the Father, to fulfill the law completely.

112
00:57:45.434 --> 00:57:51.434
And even the temptations of Satan, every time could say this by saying, it is written.

113
00:57:51.434 --> 00:57:53.434
It is written.

114
00:57:53.434 --> 00:57:56.434
Jesus was the perfect lamb. Amen?

115
00:57:57.434 --> 00:58:04.434
And so, because we humans, as Paul writes in Romans,

116
00:58:04.434 --> 00:58:10.434
because we humans have all fallen short of the glory of God,

117
00:58:10.434 --> 00:58:16.434
we cannot function as someone who is acquitted by God,

118
00:58:16.434 --> 00:58:18.434
based on our deeds.

119
00:58:18.434 --> 00:58:21.434
No one. Absolutely no one. And then all of us not.

120
00:58:21.434 --> 00:58:28.434
But what Jesus has done is, he died on a cross for your and my sin.

121
00:58:28.434 --> 00:58:34.434
And the Bible says very beautifully, through the sin that came through one man,

122
00:58:34.434 --> 00:58:39.434
salvation has also come through that other man.

123
00:58:39.434 --> 00:58:41.434
Through one man.

124
00:58:41.434 --> 00:58:46.434
Through the obedience of one man, King Jesus.

125
00:58:46.434 --> 00:58:49.434
So strong is obedience, church.

126
00:58:49.434 --> 00:58:55.434
Obedience is much stronger than you can imagine.

127
00:58:55.434 --> 00:59:02.434
Through the obedience of Jesus, you and I have come to the possibility

128
00:59:02.434 --> 00:59:05.434
to become children of God.

129
00:59:05.434 --> 00:59:07.434
To Jesus all glory and honor.

130
00:59:07.434 --> 00:59:10.434
Seriously, He is amazing.

131
00:59:10.434 --> 00:59:15.434
And so when it comes to sanctification, namely sanctified,

132
00:59:15.434 --> 00:59:19.434
it means that you are sanctified by the blood of Jesus.

133
00:59:19.434 --> 00:59:25.434
And that means that you are out of this world, with the guilt that was upon you,

134
00:59:25.434 --> 00:59:28.434
that you have been acquitted of your guilt,

135
00:59:28.434 --> 00:59:31.434
so that you can live on with God.

136
00:59:31.434 --> 00:59:38.434
And then sanctification, or holiness, means that you are set apart.

137
00:59:38.434 --> 00:59:46.434
Set apart from the guilty, you are now set apart and belong to the righteous.

138
00:59:46.434 --> 00:59:48.434
Hallelujah, praise the Lord.

139
00:59:48.434 --> 00:59:50.434
I am righteous by the name of Jesus.

140
00:59:50.434 --> 00:59:53.434
I am not righteous by my good works.

141
00:59:53.434 --> 00:59:56.434
I am not justified by how well I can preach.

142
00:59:56.434 --> 01:00:00.434
I am not justified by how good a father I can be.

143
01:00:00.434 --> 01:00:04.434
I am not justified by how much money I give to the church.

144
01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:08.434
I am justified only by the blood of Jesus.

145
01:00:08.434 --> 01:00:11.434
That must be very important.

146
01:00:11.434 --> 01:00:15.434
And then it is not just one, I explained that last week.

147
01:00:15.434 --> 01:00:18.434
It is not just one, but it is a sum of things.

148
01:00:18.434 --> 01:00:22.434
You bring all these beautiful concepts together.

149
01:00:22.434 --> 01:00:28.434
In addition, it is also true that you must be cleansed of your sins.

150
01:00:28.434 --> 01:00:32.434
And also by the blood of Jesus you are cleansed of your sins.

151
01:00:32.434 --> 01:00:41.434
But you must make this choice, this cleansing, you have to choose it to ultimately say yes to Jesus.

152
01:00:41.434 --> 01:00:46.434
You must say yes to Jesus, if he is to be able to sanctify you.

153
01:00:46.434 --> 01:00:48.434
His work is perfect.

154
01:00:48.434 --> 01:00:51.434
He has done what he had to do.

155
01:00:51.434 --> 01:00:54.434
But we must say yes to Jesus. Amen.

156
01:00:54.434 --> 01:01:01.434
For example, if you say to yourself, I do believe in Jesus, but I do not want to be baptized by Jesus.

157
01:01:01.434 --> 01:01:07.434
Then you can believe in Jesus, but you have not done what Jesus said.

158
01:01:07.434 --> 01:01:09.434
Do you understand what I mean?

159
01:01:09.434 --> 01:01:16.434
All who have heard my words and do what I have said.

160
01:01:17.434 --> 01:01:24.434
That is why Peter also says in Acts chapter 2, when a very large group of people came to Peter,

161
01:01:24.434 --> 01:01:29.434
because the disciples were praying in new tongues.

162
01:01:29.434 --> 01:01:33.434
And they were praying in all kinds of foreign languages.

163
01:01:33.434 --> 01:01:40.434
And they were praying in Polish and in German and in French and in Italian and in Dutch.

164
01:01:40.434 --> 01:01:42.434
Did not exist then, but alright.

165
01:01:42.434 --> 01:01:45.434
They were praying in all sorts of languages.

166
01:01:45.434 --> 01:01:49.434
And all those people who came to Jerusalem said, wow, what is happening here?

167
01:01:49.434 --> 01:01:52.434
Because they are praying in my own language.

168
01:01:52.434 --> 01:01:58.434
And how can it be that I hear the gospel, the good news of Jesus in my own language?

169
01:01:58.434 --> 01:02:01.434
And those people said, what is going on here?

170
01:02:01.434 --> 01:02:04.434
And Peter explains it, he explains the gospel.

171
01:02:04.434 --> 01:02:08.434
And then the people say, what should we do now?

172
01:02:08.434 --> 01:02:10.434
Do you know what Peter says then?

173
01:02:10.434 --> 01:02:14.434
Repent and be baptized.

174
01:02:14.434 --> 01:02:15.434
Voilà.

175
01:02:15.434 --> 01:02:19.434
So you must repent and be baptized.

176
01:02:19.434 --> 01:02:26.434
So it is, Jesus has done everything possible for man to come back into relationship with the Father.

177
01:02:26.434 --> 01:02:31.434
And man responds by being baptized.

178
01:02:31.434 --> 01:02:36.434
So that our sins are removed by the blood of Jesus. Amen?

179
01:02:37.434 --> 01:02:43.434
Even if Jesus had not died, you could be baptized as much as you want, but it wouldn't work.

180
01:02:43.434 --> 01:02:48.434
It is by the blood of Jesus that we are cleansed from our sins. Amen?

181
01:02:48.434 --> 01:02:56.434
Only the blood, only the sacrifice of Jesus frees us from our sins. Amen?

182
01:02:58.434 --> 01:03:04.434
And then, and this is the point I talked about with you last week, a whole sermon long.

183
01:03:04.434 --> 01:03:13.434
Then it is also true that we as Christians must dedicate ourselves.

184
01:03:13.434 --> 01:03:17.434
And that is your choice.

185
01:03:17.434 --> 01:03:25.434
And the extent to which you dedicate yourself to Jesus is all up to you.

186
01:03:25.434 --> 01:03:32.434
You can choose not to dedicate yourself to Jesus at all.

187
01:03:32.434 --> 01:03:41.434
You can choose to change yourself only a little in your thinking.

188
01:03:41.434 --> 01:03:44.434
Those three flow into each other.

189
01:03:44.434 --> 01:03:49.434
Jesus died for you, that is already prepared. That is good, that is perfect.

190
01:03:49.434 --> 01:03:52.434
Glory, hallelujah, amen. Alpha and omega.

191
01:03:52.434 --> 01:03:57.434
He who has begun a work will also complete it in you. That is completely done.

192
01:03:58.434 --> 01:04:06.434
That cleansing, Paul often talks about, that cleansing is to start thinking as new people now.

193
01:04:06.434 --> 01:04:10.434
You are a new creation through Him, but then also go and do that.

194
01:04:10.434 --> 01:04:15.434
Then also put off your old life and then also put on something new.

195
01:04:15.434 --> 01:04:19.434
Then also speak differently. Then also look differently.

196
01:04:19.434 --> 01:04:25.434
Then also treat other people differently. Then also engage with different music.

197
01:04:25.434 --> 01:04:30.434
Do not listen to the music of today anymore, but listen to the music of the Lord Jesus.

198
01:04:30.434 --> 01:04:34.434
Do not do anymore, do not go to the places where the world goes.

199
01:04:34.434 --> 01:04:41.434
In other words, we must set our lives on the right path together with God.

200
01:04:41.434 --> 01:04:45.434
And in that lies a piece of cleansing and in that lies a piece of dedication.

201
01:04:45.434 --> 01:04:48.434
That dedication and that cleansing go perfectly together.

202
01:04:48.434 --> 01:04:51.434
Do you understand what I mean?

203
01:04:51.434 --> 01:04:57.434
That dedication is an important thing I want to talk about with us as a church.

204
01:04:57.434 --> 01:05:03.434
That dedication, I don't want to be too negative,

205
01:05:03.434 --> 01:05:09.434
but the dedication is something that can sometimes be lacking in our society.

206
01:05:09.434 --> 01:05:12.434
And especially in the western churches.

207
01:05:12.434 --> 01:05:14.434
The dedication is something that can sometimes be lacking.

208
01:05:14.434 --> 01:05:18.434
Why? Because as churches, especially today,

209
01:05:18.434 --> 01:05:23.434
to not offend anyone, to not insult anyone, to not burden anyone,

210
01:05:23.434 --> 01:05:27.434
churches sometimes say, Jesus has forgiven you.

211
01:05:27.434 --> 01:05:31.434
He has forgiven you. It's all good. It's all fine. It's all nice.

212
01:05:31.434 --> 01:05:34.434
Wonderful, wonderful, wonderful. It's all fine. It's all fine.

213
01:05:34.434 --> 01:05:42.434
While the Bible is full of stories and examples and heroes of faith

214
01:05:42.434 --> 01:05:46.434
of people who laid down their lives for King Jesus.

215
01:05:46.434 --> 01:05:53.434
I am even reading a book at home, something that occurs in the history of the church,

216
01:05:53.434 --> 01:05:57.434
that is not even included in the Bible, but where the people

217
01:05:57.434 --> 01:06:03.434
in 500, 600 years after Christ, no, 600, 700 years after Christ,

218
01:06:03.434 --> 01:06:10.434
gave their lives, refusing to deny Jesus.

219
01:06:10.434 --> 01:06:15.434
But they said, I would rather die than deny the name of Jesus.

220
01:06:15.434 --> 01:06:20.434
People who laid down their lives for King Jesus.

221
01:06:20.434 --> 01:06:25.434
That is the piece of dedication I want to talk about today.

222
01:06:25.434 --> 01:06:29.434
And that dedication can be very heavy. It can cost you your life.

223
01:06:29.434 --> 01:06:33.434
On the other hand, I do not want to say that it will necessarily cost you your life,

224
01:06:33.434 --> 01:06:37.434
but at the very least you must lay down your own egocentric life.

225
01:06:37.434 --> 01:06:42.434
At the very least, you must be able to lay down everything you lived for and everything that made you happy,

226
01:06:42.434 --> 01:06:45.434
at the very least you must be able to lay that down at the cross and say,

227
01:06:45.434 --> 01:06:50.434
Lord, not my will, but Your will be done.

228
01:06:51.434 --> 01:06:54.434
Before I talk for another hour and a half without the Bible,

229
01:06:54.434 --> 01:06:58.434
let's read 1 Peter 1 and 1 Peter 2 now.

230
01:06:58.434 --> 01:07:01.434
For what Peter is saying here,

231
01:07:01.434 --> 01:07:09.434
is simply full of sanctification, purification, and consecration.

232
01:07:09.434 --> 01:07:14.434
We will read through it together and occasionally I will make a comment

233
01:07:14.434 --> 01:07:20.434
to show, look, this is that ingredient. Pay attention, pay attention.

234
01:07:20.434 --> 01:07:23.434
We start with 1 Peter 1, I will read it from the basic Bible.

235
01:07:23.434 --> 01:07:28.434
Peter, a message from Jesus Christ.

236
01:07:28.434 --> 01:07:32.434
And I can already pause to say something about that.

237
01:07:32.434 --> 01:07:35.434
Peter knew who he is.

238
01:07:35.434 --> 01:07:39.434
Peter is a messenger of Jesus Christ.

239
01:07:39.434 --> 01:07:46.434
Peter is dedicated, so you already have consecration in the first few words.

240
01:07:46.434 --> 01:07:49.434
I am Peter, he says, I am a messenger of God.

241
01:07:49.434 --> 01:07:53.434
My question to you is, who are you?

242
01:07:54.434 --> 01:07:57.434
Let's think about that for a moment.

243
01:07:57.434 --> 01:08:00.434
Who are you? Seriously.

244
01:08:00.434 --> 01:08:04.434
Stop listening to Timmetje on the stage for a moment, think for yourself.

245
01:08:04.434 --> 01:08:07.434
Who are you?

246
01:08:07.434 --> 01:08:10.434
Who are you for God?

247
01:08:10.434 --> 01:08:15.434
First of all, are you a son or daughter to God?

248
01:08:15.434 --> 01:08:21.434
And secondly, do you need a consecration, do you need a dedication to God?

249
01:08:21.434 --> 01:08:24.434
Because you must live for the Lord.

250
01:08:24.434 --> 01:08:30.434
You must lay down your body and your life and your thoughts and all your opinions before the Lord,

251
01:08:30.434 --> 01:08:32.434
so that you can live for Him.

252
01:08:32.434 --> 01:08:38.434
Because here is a point, God does not just use a few people in this church to live for Him.

253
01:08:38.434 --> 01:08:42.434
He uses everyone in His body to live for Him.

254
01:08:42.434 --> 01:08:49.434
Peter, a messenger of Jesus Christ, writes this letter to the woman.

255
01:08:49.434 --> 01:08:56.434
He writes this letter to the strangers who believe in Jesus and who live scattered abroad,

256
01:08:56.434 --> 01:09:01.434
in Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia.

257
01:09:01.434 --> 01:09:08.434
As God intended, He has called you to belong to Him.

258
01:09:08.434 --> 01:09:11.434
Called to belong to Him.

259
01:09:11.434 --> 01:09:16.434
Sanctification, purification, consecration.

260
01:09:16.434 --> 01:09:18.434
What happens when God calls you?

261
01:09:18.434 --> 01:09:23.434
Then you are called to be sanctified to come to Him.

262
01:09:23.434 --> 01:09:26.434
Through Jesus, for we will read further now.

263
01:09:26.434 --> 01:09:30.434
He wanted you to be obedient to whom?

264
01:09:30.434 --> 01:09:32.434
To Jesus Christ.

265
01:09:32.434 --> 01:09:37.434
He wanted you to be cleansed by His blood.

266
01:09:37.434 --> 01:09:39.434
What ingredient is this?

267
01:09:39.434 --> 01:09:41.434
Come on, work with me.

268
01:09:41.434 --> 01:09:43.434
Cleansing.

269
01:09:43.434 --> 01:09:47.434
And through the working of His Spirit, you now belong to God.

270
01:09:47.434 --> 01:09:49.434
What ingredient is that?

271
01:09:49.434 --> 01:09:50.434
Belonging to God?

272
01:09:50.434 --> 01:09:52.434
Sanctification, indeed.

273
01:09:52.434 --> 01:09:56.434
At first you belonged to that, now you belong to God.

274
01:09:56.434 --> 01:09:59.434
And if God is for me...

275
01:10:01.434 --> 01:10:02.434
Voilà.

276
01:10:03.434 --> 01:10:08.434
I pray that God will be good to you in more and more things.

277
01:10:08.434 --> 01:10:12.434
Also that you will have more and more of God's peace.

278
01:10:12.434 --> 01:10:19.434
We are very grateful to God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.

279
01:10:19.434 --> 01:10:22.434
For because He is so good and loving...

280
01:10:22.434 --> 01:10:23.434
Here it comes again.

281
01:10:23.434 --> 01:10:26.434
I am going to ask you what ingredient it is.

282
01:10:26.434 --> 01:10:29.434
He has made new people out of us.

283
01:10:29.434 --> 01:10:31.434
We are born again.

284
01:10:31.434 --> 01:10:35.434
Being born again is what ingredient?

285
01:10:35.434 --> 01:10:37.434
Sanctification.

286
01:10:37.434 --> 01:10:39.434
You are born again.

287
01:10:39.434 --> 01:10:46.434
He did this by raising Jesus Christ from the dead and making Him alive again.

288
01:10:46.434 --> 01:10:48.434
We have a living God. Amen.

289
01:10:48.434 --> 01:10:51.434
Because of this, we can be full of hope.

290
01:10:52.434 --> 01:10:55.434
Verse 4 is important, I have underlined it thickly.

291
01:10:55.434 --> 01:11:00.434
For now we expect an inheritance that will never lose its value.

292
01:11:00.434 --> 01:11:03.434
That inheritance is ready for you in heaven.

293
01:11:03.434 --> 01:11:05.434
Eternal life.

294
01:11:05.434 --> 01:11:09.434
God's power keeps and protects you through faith.

295
01:11:09.434 --> 01:11:14.434
So you can receive eternal life at the end of time.

296
01:11:14.434 --> 01:11:17.434
Why do I find this an important sentence?

297
01:11:17.434 --> 01:11:19.434
Shall I tell you something?

298
01:11:19.434 --> 01:11:22.434
It is not one of the ingredients that I want to attach to this.

299
01:11:22.434 --> 01:11:25.434
I want to show with this verse.

300
01:11:25.434 --> 01:11:31.434
To be very honest, you should expect very little from this life.

301
01:11:32.434 --> 01:11:37.434
For our inheritance is waiting for us in heaven.

302
01:11:37.434 --> 01:11:47.434
And the sooner you get there, the more you can say to yourself, I actually expect nothing from this life.

303
01:11:47.434 --> 01:11:55.434
For in faith and devotion, I can give myself to God.

304
01:11:55.434 --> 01:12:00.434
In faith for what awaits me in heaven.

305
01:12:02.434 --> 01:12:06.434
And this is important that I pause here for a moment.

306
01:12:06.434 --> 01:12:14.434
For if your hope is fully placed in the rewards of this life,

307
01:12:14.434 --> 01:12:21.434
you run the risk of being disappointed in the things of this life.

308
01:12:21.434 --> 01:12:24.434
Today you have a good business.

309
01:12:24.434 --> 01:12:27.434
Tomorrow some virus happens.

310
01:12:27.434 --> 01:12:31.434
You find yourself in a lockdown, you go bankrupt.

311
01:12:31.434 --> 01:12:39.434
If you thought that God is your God who is supposed to make you rich in your business,

312
01:12:39.434 --> 01:12:43.434
and tomorrow you go bankrupt, where is your faith then?

313
01:12:45.434 --> 01:12:54.434
Maybe you believe in God and you have children who at this moment have not yet chosen Jesus.

314
01:12:54.434 --> 01:13:00.434
I don't want to ask the church, raise your hands, but keep praying for your family.

315
01:13:00.434 --> 01:13:05.434
But here you stand as a father or as a husband and you go for the Lord.

316
01:13:05.434 --> 01:13:08.434
And you believe that God will protect you.

317
01:13:08.434 --> 01:13:13.434
But something happens in the free will of your spouse or your children,

318
01:13:13.434 --> 01:13:16.434
and they are not walking with the Lord at that moment.

319
01:13:16.434 --> 01:13:20.434
And you have been praying for years, Lord save them, Lord save them, Lord save them.

320
01:13:20.434 --> 01:13:23.434
And it still doesn't happen, and it still doesn't happen.

321
01:13:23.434 --> 01:13:30.434
If your hope is completely placed on all the gifts you want to receive from God in this life,

322
01:13:30.434 --> 01:13:36.434
you will quickly find yourself deceived and can become disappointed in the things of God.

323
01:13:36.434 --> 01:13:42.434
For God indeed says here in 1 Peter that a reward awaits us in heaven.

324
01:13:44.434 --> 01:13:46.434
Yes, God will protect you.

325
01:13:46.434 --> 01:13:49.434
Yes, we can pray for forgiveness and healing.

326
01:13:49.434 --> 01:13:51.434
Yes, we can pray for protection.

327
01:13:51.434 --> 01:13:56.434
Every evening when I go to bed and fall asleep, I pray for my family.

328
01:13:56.434 --> 01:14:02.434
I declare the blood of Jesus over my house, over my children, over myself, over my wife.

329
01:14:02.434 --> 01:14:08.434
And I always pray, Lord send your angels around my house and even position them in my house,

330
01:14:08.434 --> 01:14:11.434
so that no harm will come to me.

331
01:14:11.434 --> 01:14:13.434
Of course I believe in that.

332
01:14:13.434 --> 01:14:19.434
At the same time, I also know that millions of Christians have been murdered for the name of Jesus.

333
01:14:19.434 --> 01:14:24.434
At the same time, I also know that I have prayed for people who were sick.

334
01:14:24.434 --> 01:14:29.434
And I have seen healing happen in the name of Jesus through my prayer.

335
01:14:29.434 --> 01:14:32.434
Not to boast about myself, for it is in the name of Jesus.

336
01:14:32.434 --> 01:14:36.434
But I have also prayed for people who did not receive healing.

337
01:14:36.434 --> 01:14:39.434
Do I still have faith in King Jesus?

338
01:14:40.434 --> 01:14:42.434
I will tell you this, dear people.

339
01:14:42.434 --> 01:14:45.434
I will always continue to pray for healing for people.

340
01:14:45.434 --> 01:14:46.434
For the rest of my life.

341
01:14:46.434 --> 01:14:49.434
Even if I see it happening, even if I don't see it happening.

342
01:14:49.434 --> 01:14:53.434
It is not my experience on which I build my faith.

343
01:14:53.434 --> 01:14:55.434
I build my faith on the Bible.

344
01:14:55.434 --> 01:14:59.434
And when the Bible says, by His stripes we are healed,

345
01:14:59.434 --> 01:15:04.434
I base my faith on what is written in the Bible and not on what I have seen myself.

346
01:15:04.434 --> 01:15:07.434
For who says that what I have seen is the truth?

347
01:15:10.434 --> 01:15:11.434
Dear people.

348
01:15:11.434 --> 01:15:15.434
Do not expect too much from this life.

349
01:15:17.434 --> 01:15:21.434
This life is a Romans chapter 8 life.

350
01:15:22.434 --> 01:15:28.434
Great things happen and incredibly terrible things happen.

351
01:15:29.434 --> 01:15:34.434
My faith is in what awaits me in heaven.

352
01:15:35.434 --> 01:15:39.434
And if I can commit myself to that, then I can do that too.

353
01:15:39.434 --> 01:15:44.434
And if I can commit myself to that, then I have a piece of dedication in hand.

354
01:15:45.434 --> 01:15:47.434
Then I have dedication in hand.

355
01:15:49.434 --> 01:15:54.434
When we as youth leaders will soon be leading a youth camp in a few days.

356
01:15:55.434 --> 01:15:59.434
Do you think all the teenagers will behave perfectly?

357
01:15:59.434 --> 01:16:04.434
Do you think all the teenagers will come to repentance during that camp?

358
01:16:04.434 --> 01:16:10.434
Do you think all problems will disappear like snow in the sun for all the teenagers, for all situations?

359
01:16:10.434 --> 01:16:13.434
That they will never do anything wrong again afterwards?

360
01:16:13.434 --> 01:16:16.434
If that is the case, then we can start charging money for such a camp.

361
01:16:19.434 --> 01:16:20.434
But that's not how it works.

362
01:16:20.434 --> 01:16:23.434
But why do we youth leaders and children's leaders do what we do?

363
01:16:23.434 --> 01:16:28.434
Because we believe that the prize is still ahead.

364
01:16:29.434 --> 01:16:35.434
And that we dedicate ourselves to do what we believe in the spiritual world.

365
01:16:35.434 --> 01:16:37.434
Not in the natural world.

366
01:16:37.434 --> 01:16:40.434
In the natural world, you can get a big mouth from such a teenager.

367
01:16:40.434 --> 01:16:43.434
Why? Because they have a little backpack on.

368
01:16:43.434 --> 01:16:47.434
But in the spiritual world, we see young people coming to Christ.

369
01:16:47.434 --> 01:16:49.434
Maybe now, maybe tomorrow.

370
01:16:49.434 --> 01:16:54.434
Maybe that seed still needs to die and it will take another ten years until it comes to the revelation of Christ.

371
01:16:54.434 --> 01:16:58.434
And they may only come to repentance much later, at the age of thirty.

372
01:16:58.434 --> 01:17:01.434
And that's why we have been putting in all that effort with all those teenagers.

373
01:17:01.434 --> 01:17:04.434
While we have not yet seen the fruit.

374
01:17:04.434 --> 01:17:05.434
Do you understand what I mean?

375
01:17:05.434 --> 01:17:09.434
This is a model for what I want to share with you, also about your own life.

376
01:17:09.434 --> 01:17:17.434
And that is why Peter stumbles here that we must have an expectation for what is prepared for us in heaven.

377
01:17:19.434 --> 01:17:20.434
Let's continue.

378
01:17:20.434 --> 01:17:21.434
Verse 6.

379
01:17:21.434 --> 01:17:24.434
Be glad about that.

380
01:17:24.434 --> 01:17:29.434
Even though your faith is tested in various ways.

381
01:17:29.434 --> 01:17:34.434
But this will show whether your faith is genuine.

382
01:17:34.434 --> 01:17:36.434
Are you reading those words with me?

383
01:17:36.434 --> 01:17:41.434
Genuine faith is more precious than pure gold.

384
01:17:41.434 --> 01:17:42.434
Do you see that?

385
01:17:42.434 --> 01:17:46.434
Do not chase after gold, chase after Jesus.

386
01:17:46.434 --> 01:17:48.434
And believe who he is.

387
01:17:48.434 --> 01:17:51.434
Gold is refined in the fire...

388
01:17:51.434 --> 01:17:53.434
What does it say here, what ingredient?

389
01:17:53.434 --> 01:17:55.434
Purification.

390
01:17:55.434 --> 01:17:58.434
Gold is purified in the fire.

391
01:17:58.434 --> 01:18:04.434
In the same way, your faith is refined by the fire of difficulties.

392
01:18:04.434 --> 01:18:07.434
Let's take a look at this for a moment.

393
01:18:10.434 --> 01:18:11.434
Do we have that in front of me?

394
01:18:11.434 --> 01:18:12.434
Yes.

395
01:18:12.434 --> 01:18:13.434
Can we read this sentence for a moment?

396
01:18:13.434 --> 01:18:19.434
In the same way, your faith is refined by the fire of difficulties.

397
01:18:19.434 --> 01:18:23.434
This does not fit in our denomination at all.

398
01:18:25.434 --> 01:18:27.434
Please read this sentence for a moment.

399
01:18:31.434 --> 01:18:33.434
The fire of difficulties?

400
01:18:33.434 --> 01:18:35.434
Where is this?

401
01:18:35.434 --> 01:18:37.434
Why is that here?

402
01:18:37.434 --> 01:18:46.434
Why does Peter say that we go through a fire of difficulties and that this purifies our faith?

403
01:18:46.434 --> 01:18:52.434
I thought Jesus did it all for us, didn't he?

404
01:18:52.434 --> 01:18:54.434
100%.

405
01:18:54.434 --> 01:18:58.434
But I thought we are only cleansed by the blood of Jesus and through the Bible?

406
01:18:58.434 --> 01:19:00.434
Yes, 100%.

407
01:19:00.434 --> 01:19:06.434
But when you are going through difficulties, that faith is put under pressure.

408
01:19:06.434 --> 01:19:13.434
And when that faith is under pressure, how committed are you to your faith,

409
01:19:13.434 --> 01:19:21.434
by saying what I see happening in my life must not be out of balance with what I believe in King Jesus.

410
01:19:21.434 --> 01:19:25.434
And that is the difficulties Peter is talking about.

411
01:19:25.434 --> 01:19:34.434
Even if they put a gun to your head and say to you, you must now give up Jesus or the trigger will be pulled.

412
01:19:34.434 --> 01:19:37.434
What do you do in that difficulty?

413
01:19:37.434 --> 01:19:39.434
Stand for Jesus.

414
01:19:39.434 --> 01:19:45.434
And of course I bring up the hardest example here, but we go through difficulties every day.

415
01:19:45.434 --> 01:19:54.434
Lack of money, lack of respect, lack of honor from others, lack of understanding from your family, lack of so much.

416
01:19:54.434 --> 01:20:02.434
And Peter says, hold on to your faith, hold on to your faith, be committed to your faith, be committed to your faith.

417
01:20:02.434 --> 01:20:10.434
For then it will ultimately be shown that you have gone through the fire of difficulties and that you will stand pure before the Lord. Amen.

418
01:20:14.434 --> 01:20:20.434
And when Jesus Christ returns, you will be praised by him for your pure faith.

419
01:20:23.434 --> 01:20:26.434
You have never seen him, yet you love him.

420
01:20:26.434 --> 01:20:31.434
You believe in him and are very glad that you have been saved through him.

421
01:20:31.434 --> 01:20:35.434
What ingredient is this? This is sanctification.

422
01:20:35.434 --> 01:20:39.434
And being saved is indeed the goal of faith.

423
01:20:41.434 --> 01:20:46.434
Then Peter says something about this gospel for a few verses, how important it is. Verse 10.

424
01:20:46.434 --> 01:20:52.434
The prophets have already prophesied about that salvation. They tried to understand how that salvation would come.

425
01:20:52.434 --> 01:20:55.434
It is indeed so complex what Jesus has done.

426
01:20:55.434 --> 01:20:59.434
The Spirit of God had already told them that Christ would have to suffer.

427
01:20:59.434 --> 01:21:05.434
He had also told them about the heavenly power and majesty that he would have afterwards.

428
01:21:05.434 --> 01:21:08.434
Then, in heaven. The reward would come afterwards.

429
01:21:08.434 --> 01:21:12.434
But they did not understand when that would be and how it would happen exactly.

430
01:21:12.434 --> 01:21:16.434
It is powerful what is written there. It is deep what is written there.

431
01:21:17.434 --> 01:21:21.434
But God showed them that they did not need to understand it themselves.

432
01:21:22.434 --> 01:21:29.434
What they said about it was meant for the people who would live after them, namely us.

433
01:21:29.434 --> 01:21:36.434
They were already speaking about the things that you have now heard from the people who brought you the good news.

434
01:21:36.434 --> 01:21:42.434
Through the Holy Spirit who has come from heaven, they made that good news known to you.

435
01:21:42.434 --> 01:21:47.434
And the good news, check this sentence that is written there. One of my favorite sentences in this letter.

436
01:21:47.434 --> 01:21:52.434
And the good news is so amazing that even the angels want to know more about it.

437
01:21:52.434 --> 01:21:57.434
So deep and so powerful is the gospel of Jesus Christ.

438
01:21:57.434 --> 01:22:03.434
That all of creation is watching what Jesus has done.

439
01:22:03.434 --> 01:22:07.434
What intense things Jesus has done.

440
01:22:07.434 --> 01:22:14.434
That even the angels, the mighty holy angels of God, are allowed to look.

441
01:22:14.434 --> 01:22:21.434
And that they are just standing there watching how God plays this out for the angelic powers.

442
01:22:21.434 --> 01:22:24.434
Amazing. Hallelujah.

443
01:22:24.434 --> 01:22:29.434
Verse 13, here comes that consecration, here comes dedication.

444
01:22:29.434 --> 01:22:35.434
So keep your mind sharp and pay close attention.

445
01:22:35.434 --> 01:22:41.434
Trust completely that God will take good care of you on the day that Jesus returns.

446
01:22:41.434 --> 01:22:45.434
Do not listen anymore to the desires of your old self.

447
01:22:45.434 --> 01:22:51.434
Cleansing. Those are still from the time when you knew nothing of the good news.

448
01:22:51.434 --> 01:22:56.434
Do you see here how Peter is playing out these three ingredients?

449
01:22:56.434 --> 01:23:01.434
Sanctification is actually from the time before you wanted to know anything about Jesus.

450
01:23:01.434 --> 01:23:05.434
And now through Jesus, you do want to know something about Jesus.

451
01:23:05.434 --> 01:23:10.434
Here is a good barometer for your heart. Check this.

452
01:23:11.434 --> 01:23:21.434
What it says here means that if you have zero desire to think about Jesus throughout the whole week,

453
01:23:21.434 --> 01:23:24.434
to thank Him, to love Him.

454
01:23:24.434 --> 01:23:30.434
If you go through the whole week, in creation,

455
01:23:30.434 --> 01:23:36.434
before meals, while watching your children, reflecting on your own salvation, whatever it may be.

456
01:23:36.434 --> 01:23:44.434
If you never think of Jesus all week long, what it says here means that you want to live for Him.

457
01:23:44.434 --> 01:23:51.434
If you don't have that at all, I would like to ask you to please think about your salvation.

458
01:23:51.434 --> 01:23:55.434
Oh Tim, that's pretty intense.

459
01:23:55.434 --> 01:23:59.434
That comes because we are trained in the Western church by saying, it's all good.

460
01:23:59.434 --> 01:24:03.434
Come to church, it's all good. No, that's not what it says here.

461
01:24:03.434 --> 01:24:07.434
Here it says that you must live as you want to.

462
01:24:07.434 --> 01:24:12.434
That you want to be with Him. That you no longer want to sin.

463
01:24:12.434 --> 01:24:15.434
I no longer want to sin.

464
01:24:15.434 --> 01:24:21.434
I have sinned so much, I know how it goes, I am an expert in sin, but I do not want it anymore.

465
01:24:21.434 --> 01:24:27.434
So if you do not want this anymore, then you are in that evangelical corner.

466
01:24:27.434 --> 01:24:32.434
Then you are in the corner that you have been set free and that you have been sanctified.

467
01:24:32.434 --> 01:24:37.434
You no longer belong in the camp of the desires of your old self.

468
01:24:37.434 --> 01:24:42.434
But you now belong in the camp of the righteous to Him.

469
01:24:42.434 --> 01:24:44.434
Praise God.

470
01:24:44.434 --> 01:24:46.434
Where was I?

471
01:24:46.434 --> 01:24:48.434
14 Dooms.

472
01:24:48.434 --> 01:24:50.434
Do not listen to the desires of your old self anymore.

473
01:24:50.434 --> 01:24:54.434
Those are still from the time when you knew nothing of the Good News.

474
01:24:54.434 --> 01:24:59.434
But now listen as obedient children to God.

475
01:24:59.434 --> 01:25:04.434
Dedication. He has called you to live for Him.

476
01:25:04.434 --> 01:25:10.434
Dedication. God is holy, therefore you must also live holy in everything you do.

477
01:25:10.434 --> 01:25:15.434
Dedication, cleansing, sanctification. It is all in those verses.

478
01:25:15.434 --> 01:25:18.434
For it is written in the books, shall we say this together?

479
01:25:18.434 --> 01:25:22.434
Live holy, for I am holy. Let's say it again.

480
01:25:22.434 --> 01:25:26.434
Live holy, for I am holy. Hallelujah.

481
01:25:27.434 --> 01:25:29.434
You may call on Him as Father for help.

482
01:25:29.434 --> 01:25:34.434
He does not show favoritism, but judges all people according to what they have done.

483
01:25:34.434 --> 01:25:41.434
What? Then live in awe of Him, as long as you are here as what?

484
01:25:41.434 --> 01:25:44.434
As strangers living on earth.

485
01:25:44.434 --> 01:25:47.434
You are no longer of the world.

486
01:25:47.434 --> 01:25:52.434
There is an old Christian saying that often goes around as a cliché in the church.

487
01:25:52.434 --> 01:25:56.434
You are in the world, but you are not of the world.

488
01:25:56.434 --> 01:25:58.434
Do you understand this? Wonderful.

489
01:25:58.434 --> 01:26:07.434
He has redeemed you, sanctification from the futile way of life that you inherited from your ancestors.

490
01:26:07.434 --> 01:26:12.434
